<title>CANADA: CWB forecasts world wheat supply and dispositions.</title>
<headline>CWB forecasts world wheat supply and dispositions.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board on Monday detailed its forecast for world wheat supply and disposition in the 1996/97 (Aug/July) and 1997/98 (Aug/July) crop years in millions of tonnes.</p>
<p>		  WORLD WHEAT SUPPLY AND DISPOSITIONS</p>
<p>		  1995/96     1996/97    1997/98</p>
<p>Carry-in	  110	    96	  106</p>
<p>Production	541	   578	  575</p>
<p>Total Supply    651	   674	  681</p>
<p>Total Use	 556	   568	  570</p>
<p>Carry-out	  95	   106	  111</p>
<p>Stocks to Use    17 pct	19 pct     19 pct</p>
<p>World Trade	89	    93	   93</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
